# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.data/
runtime*/
artifacts/
Secrets/
*.sqlite*
*.db
*.db-*
*.clixml
*.pem
*.key
*.enc
*.bin
*.log
*.lnk
*.jsonl
*.exe
*.dll
*.pdb
*.i64
*.idb
*.id0
*.id1
*.id2
*.dmp
*.dump
*.pcap*
*.obj
*.lib
*.exp
*.ilk
*.zip
build/
dist/

.dart_tool/
.idea/
*.iml
bin/
obj/
ephemeral/
*.tar*
*.7z
*.spf*
*.dat

# Machine-specific deployment endpoints and private settings
/config/network.json
**/settings.private.json
# Local protocol debugging screenshots (source and analysis remain tracked)
/protocol/nixiang/**/*.png
